    "id": "cvpr26-c48ceca9041b",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-c48ceca9041b",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Our method distills a pre-trained teacher model, denoted as sdata, into a few-step video generator Gœâ. The training procedure consists of the following steps:(1) A batch of real video-text pairs is sampled from the dataset. After applying noise perturbations to the videos, the student model performs denoising reconstruction. A regression loss is computed between the reconstructed video and the ground-truth video. Subsequently, this loss is adaptively weighted using our Loss Mean Cache to produce the Ô¨Ånal adaptive regression loss (see Sec. 3.3 for details). (2) Text conditions are sampled from the dataset to guide the student model in generating a video from pure noise. The denoised output from this process is used to compute a temporal regularization loss (Eq. 8) and a distribution matching loss (Eq. 4).(3) Finally, the generator Gœâ is updated via gradient descent using the combined losses. The sgen,Œµ in DMD are updated separately, following the methodology of DMD2 (this particular update step is not depicted in the Ô¨Ågure for clarity).",
