      "id": "cvpr26-ef116d950c84",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the proposed Affordance-First Decomposition (AFD) framework for continual video‚Äìlanguage question answering. A stream of video‚Äìlanguage tasks arrives over time, each video is encoded and mapped by a shared affordance head into slowly varying affordance tokens and prototypes, while questions are embedded and stored for replay to route per-layer LoRA adapters in the LLM-backbone scheduler. Stability loss Laff acts only on the affordance head, whereas task and replay losses (Ltask + Lreplay) act only on the routed adapters, explicitly separating a stable affordance substrate from a plastic reasoning module.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
        91.80099487304688,
        330.8919677734375,
        520.20166015625,
