      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3 : Overview of SpeciaRL Given an input image I I , the policy model generates N N open-ended predictions { p 1 , ‚Ä¶ , p N } \\{p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}\\} . Each prediction is categorized by a judge model (LLM verifier) as wrong or correct at different levels of specificity with respect to the ground-truth. A verifiable reward r i ‚àó r_{i}^{*} is then assigned according to whether the prediction‚Äôs category c i c_{i} meets the adaptive reference level c ‚àó c^{*} , which is defined based on the best prediction within the N N rollouts. The resulting graded rewards are aggregated through a Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) update to reinforce policies that are maximally specific while remaining correct.",
