    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Our training process is divided into two stages: the Reference Clip ( C ‚Äã l ‚Äã i ‚Äã p 0 Clip_{0} ) Training Stage and Source Clip ( C ‚Äã l ‚Äã i ‚Äã p n ‚àà [ 1 , N ‚àí 1 ] Clip_{n\\in[1,N-1]} ) Training Stage. In Reference Clip¬†Training Stage, anchors A 0 A_{0} are initialized by the fused point cloud from all frames of C ‚Äã l ‚Äã i ‚Äã p 0 Clip_{0} . The anchors are fed into a spatio-temporal field ( S ‚Äã T ‚Äã F 0 STF_{0} ) to extract dynamic features, which are then concatenated with static features. They are decoded to Temporal Gaussian attributes and rendered via rasterization. In Source Clip¬†Training Stage, we inherit the anchors, decoder and the static features from Reference Clip. Residual anchors are computed between the current and Reference Clip A 0 A_{0} . Finally, the same training pipeline as in the Reference Clip¬† stage is applied using the A n A_{n} conpensated with residual anchors and the newly initialized S ‚Äã T ‚Äã F STF .",
