      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : The overall pipeline of the proposed FinPercep-RM and Co-evolutionary Curriculum Learning (CCL) framework. FinPercep-RM produces a Fine-grained Perceptual Degradation Map that captures spatially localized defect likelihood and intensity, and the reward model is progressively expanded from small-variance, coarse-grained rewards to large-variance, fine-grained signals. During training, under the CCL mechanism, the Generator first learns with the coarse global reward from R ‚Äã M 0 RM_{0} for a stable and easy initialization, and is then co-evolutionarily guided by increasingly strict R ‚Äã M k RM_{k} versions to enhance local fidelity and suppress reward hacking.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2512.22647v2/pipline-ready.png",
